Arch-lich pets are hazardous as there is nothing that you can do that
will increase the tameness of your arch-lich.  Once it goes feral it
will either be hostile or not.  If hostile, you could have big
problems, especially without MR.  At best, if the arch-lich goes feral
but stays peaceful it will teleport next to you and block your way in
passages, which is very annoying and potentially dangerous.

My advice is to leave the arch-lich in the mines when you are done
with that branch.  You're a valkyrie, you don't need such a hazardous
pet.  Get yourself a nice purple worm or D or T or something.  If you
do keep the pet, make sure that it picks up a unicorn horn; I lost a
good hero to a confused arch-lich before.

